1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,060
For two months, many of you have been trying desperately to convince me that I would like something that I was pretty confident I wouldn't.

2
00:00:09,619 --> 00:00:15,480
And like a stubborn child refusing to even try ahead of broccoli, I stuck to my guns.

3
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:20,539
Crossed my arms and said, no, thank you. I do not like green eggs in ham.

4
00:00:21,219 --> 00:00:28,519
And for two months, I'd been adamant that I will not watch the movie that blew up this summer.

5
00:00:28,519 --> 00:00:35,539
K-pop demon hunters. I saw, I think it was two of the trailers. Maybe it was one and I saw it twice. I can't remember.

6
00:00:36,039 --> 00:00:42,240
But I saw the trailer. The animation looked great, but it is just not my kind of movie. It is a musical.

7
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:47,880
And I've been very public about how much I do not like musicals.

8
00:00:48,179 --> 00:00:56,100
So it just, it simply was not for me. But when this Netflix film exploded with popularity, I said,

9
00:00:56,100 --> 00:01:02,939
I'm happy that you're all happy. I'm glad. And for two months, they said, no Charles. Listen, you old scrooge.

10
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:09,799
This is, this is fucking incredible stuff. You might not like musicals. You might not be the biggest K-pop fan.

11
00:01:10,219 --> 00:01:17,140
But this movie is going to blow you away. Trust me. The amount of times I heard that if I only had a nickel.

12
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:23,120
And I was firmly planting my feet and lat spreading saying, I'm not doing it.

13
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:28,719
You won't get me to watch it. I already know. I won't like it that much. What's the point?

14
00:01:29,359 --> 00:01:35,099
But then tonight at 5am after another sleepless evening, no rest.

15
00:01:35,299 --> 00:01:41,120
Gotta tell you sports fans, I wish the K-pop stars could start targeting Insomnia.

16
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:46,280
Fucking banish that to the shadow realm, please. If you finish with the demons, please go after Insomnia.

17
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:52,219
I'm really fucking tired of it. But I said, you know, to hell with it, I'll take a peek.

18
00:01:52,219 --> 00:01:57,379
I'll take a gander, see what all the fuss is about. You know, nothing to lose.

19
00:01:57,739 --> 00:02:03,519
I either watch something and I'm moderately entertained. I watch it and I end up loving it.

20
00:02:03,879 --> 00:02:10,659
Or I fall asleep. All of these are fine outcomes at 5am when I just can't sleep in the first place.

21
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:14,120
So I just finished it. It is now 6.30am.

22
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:20,379
And I bet you're expecting me to have like this big like Yerika come to Jesus moment like, no, you are alright.

23
00:02:20,379 --> 00:02:24,039
It actually was like my favorite animated movie ever. So I had to say that's not the case.

24
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:28,879
I feel exactly how I expected to feel after finishing this film.

25
00:02:29,259 --> 00:02:32,479
I didn't hate it or anything. I didn't dislike the movie.

26
00:02:32,879 --> 00:02:36,639
But I didn't love it or anything. It was a fine time.

27
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:41,840
It was a beautiful animated movie. Like the animation was stunning.

28
00:02:42,199 --> 00:02:47,300
I love the style of the film, which I also knew I would going into it because the trailers,

29
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:50,879
they do a really good job of setting you up for exactly what you're going to get.

30
00:02:51,219 --> 00:02:53,979
But like I said, I just don't like musicals.

31
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:57,800
And I don't dislike K-pop, but it's not my favorite musical genre.

32
00:02:58,039 --> 00:03:05,039
So it's a musical in a genre of music that I don't typically download and snap my fingers to.

33
00:03:06,099 --> 00:03:11,020
So it was never going to be like the Grand Slam home run in my eyes,

34
00:03:11,099 --> 00:03:14,819
but I totally understand why so many people have fallen head over heels and love with it.

35
00:03:14,819 --> 00:03:19,099
I definitely get it. If you like K-pop, this definitely has it out the wazoo.

36
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:23,199
And the songs are catchy. Like some of the tunes are definitely a little earworms

37
00:03:23,199 --> 00:03:25,219
that'll have you humming it a little bit, no doubt.

38
00:03:25,759 --> 00:03:31,960
My favorite song was actually the second to last one, the your idol one from the Saja Boys.

39
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:34,860
That was a good song. I enjoyed that bowler jam.

40
00:03:35,159 --> 00:03:38,680
And I'd confidently say that there's no bad songs in here.

41
00:03:38,759 --> 00:03:43,400
There's none of them where I was like plugging my ears, begging for the baggy need to stop or anything.

42
00:03:44,259 --> 00:03:46,259
Overall, like it was fine.

43
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:50,759
It's exactly what I expected to happen for me. I watched it.

44
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:59,780
I was entertained, but it wasn't something that all maybe singing or really thinking about like in a day or two from now.

45
00:04:00,639 --> 00:04:04,460
But like I said, I really do get why so many people have been glued to it.

46
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:09,419
I know it just went to theaters. Netflix. This was so big for Netflix.

47
00:04:09,419 --> 00:04:16,519
They decided to put it into theaters. And in its debut a few days ago, it brought in 18 million.

48
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:20,800
I think it was on its opening, which is actually a huge opening.

49
00:04:21,319 --> 00:04:25,120
Like it beat weapons, which I know weapons is going into like a second or third week.

50
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:29,160
But like this is a pretty big movie across the board.

51
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:33,959
And it also does something that I actually think is a pretty cool direction for movies to go.

52
00:04:33,959 --> 00:04:37,439
I've heard they've offered like sing along performances.

53
00:04:37,759 --> 00:04:49,560
Like theaters are doing sing along showings where people go in with the full notion that there will be people in the audience singing along to the music in the movie.

54
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:53,660
I would never want to be in one of those auditoriums.

55
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:59,040
Like they did that same shit with Minecraft with a block party edition, especially like Gial memes at the screen or whatever.

56
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:02,899
I would never want to be in one of these auditoriums.

57
00:05:03,319 --> 00:05:14,180
But I appreciate that they're doing it because I think any effort to make things more social and get people to interact with other people of similar interest is a great step in the right direction.

58
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:21,420
Whereas all of society and all of big business is right now focused on trying to keep you indoors and isolated from other human beings.

59
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:26,040
Even going as far as to try and fill your romantic void with AI companions.

60
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:33,459
So anything that kind of kicks that trend is getting too big thumbs up from me.

61
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:46,279
So I really like that demon hunt or K-pop demon hunters is having these sing alongs which apparently are doing really well with a bunch of people going around others with similar interest and being social and singing to a movie that they really like.

62
00:05:46,519 --> 00:05:47,720
I think that's great.

63
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:52,920
I will never go, but I'm happy that it's there and I'm glad so many people are going.

64
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:55,579
I guess I'll give you a little pseudo review here.

65
00:05:56,120 --> 00:06:06,699
The story is throughout time there have been these chosen singers who use their voice to seal demons away to keep humanity safe from them.

66
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:14,319
They use their voice as a means of keeping them at bay and the ultimate demon lord from consuming souls.

67
00:06:14,319 --> 00:06:30,660
And now in the modern era it is a K-pop group that takes on this responsibility and they're getting very close to the golden seal that will once and for all in this battle where the demons will no longer be able to access the human world at all.

68
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:34,819
Whereas in the past there's always been like little tears where they can kind of trickle in here and there.

69
00:06:35,379 --> 00:06:39,420
But now they're very close to stopping it entirely.

70
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:42,579
So we follow their journey to accomplishing that.

71
00:06:43,540 --> 00:06:47,079
Spoiler alert, we're going to get into spoilers even for K-pop demon hunters baby.

72
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:52,600
The main singer, Rumi, she is actually part demon.

73
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:59,060
And she wants to seal this so that way her demon patterns can go away.

74
00:06:59,259 --> 00:07:09,399
She's been hiding them her whole life and her mother figure who's not her actual mother but someone who promised to take care of her has been trying to keep that secret from the rest of the group and the rest of the world.

75
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:12,839
Because she believes it is a problem that needs to be fixed.

76
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:19,699
In pursuit of the golden sealing of the demons, the demons throw one last Hail Mary.

77
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:28,660
They're about to face defeat but then they call upon their own boy band who then goes to the human world and directly challenges them on the charts.

78
00:07:29,019 --> 00:07:35,480
They can't beat them in a fight because the K-pop demon hunters are very adept at combat and the fights I think are very cool.

79
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:41,139
I think the fighting is very flashy and it's very stylistic and I think it goes hard.

80
00:07:41,459 --> 00:07:46,100
There's not a lot of fighting or anything that really is mainly about the story, the characters and the music.

81
00:07:46,519 --> 00:07:48,660
But when there is fighting, I think it looks really cool.

82
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:51,240
Really everything in the movie looks very cool.

83
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:54,899
They did pull out all the stops here in the animation department.

84
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:57,680
I really appreciate that because I fucking love animation.

85
00:07:57,959 --> 00:08:01,100
It really is visually great. It is breathtaking at points.

86
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:05,279
But anyway, they have the boy band out there and now they're competing directly on the charts.

87
00:08:05,899 --> 00:08:11,660
And the demon hunter group, the K-pop demon hunters, their huntrix, that's their name.

88
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:17,660
They immediately recognize the Sajibois as being demons and they're immediately privy to their plan.

89
00:08:17,839 --> 00:08:21,740
Of stealing fans away so that way they can poke holes into the seal.

90
00:08:22,019 --> 00:08:24,680
That way the demons can flood in and power up the demon lord.

91
00:08:25,639 --> 00:08:33,639
And then a romance blossoms where the lead demon of the Sajibois and the lead of huntrix, Rumi,

92
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:38,179
they start to find common ground because she's part demon.

93
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:42,320
And he's very troubled. He doesn't want to be like evil.

94
00:08:42,799 --> 00:08:47,340
He made a mistake in his past and he has been paying for it for four centuries now.

95
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:51,019
And he just wants the voices in his head to stop.

96
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:53,480
That's the whole reason he's helping the demon guy.

97
00:08:53,480 --> 00:09:03,820
And they are at odds but eventually it blossoms into a very understanding, mutual relationship between the two of them.

98
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:09,820
And it's a decent story. Like it's not anything new. It's nothing you haven't seen before.

99
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:14,740
But it's executed well enough that I think a lot of people will find it to be very fresh.

100
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:20,480
I do think though that there were things that they wanted to explore but ran out of budget for.

101
00:09:20,759 --> 00:09:26,759
For example, Rumi, we only get little tidally wings about her past.

102
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:32,740
She is the only person of her kind that we know of in this world that is half demon, half human.

103
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:43,039
And we only know the bare bones that her mother and a demon got together and she was born and was viewed as a big mistake.

104
00:09:43,039 --> 00:09:52,799
But the mother asked for a promise from her most trusted companion to keep her daughter safe.

105
00:09:53,379 --> 00:09:57,620
But we don't know anything about the mother or the demon father or anything like that.

106
00:09:57,720 --> 00:10:01,279
And I thought for sure that would be something we've learned a little bit about but it never came.

107
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:07,620
Unless there was a post-credit scene that I might have missed. I didn't go through the entire credits. Maybe it's possible, I'm not sure.

108
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:10,139
But I'm just surprised that that wasn't explored.

109
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:16,460
It also felt like Rumi was the only character that got real depth. The other two members of Huntrix.

110
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:25,600
They kind of just played on the sidelines. They gave you bits and pieces. They gave you the general character personalities and a bit of the background.

111
00:10:25,759 --> 00:10:36,440
But never really too much. You never really got to know them very well. Past their desire to seal the demons away and their complete hatred of demons.

112
00:10:37,259 --> 00:10:45,620
I really thought this movie was going to go in a different direction towards the end too because we know Genu, that's the demon guy's name, the lead of the Sajiboyz.

113
00:10:46,039 --> 00:10:52,700
We know about his past a lot. And it seems like he's not the only one of his kind that is just reluctantly serving the demon king.

114
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:58,659
Like no one seems to want to do that. They just have the voice in their head that is compelling them to do so.

115
00:10:58,659 --> 00:11:08,039
And he explains to Rumi that all demons do is feel all of their shame and all of that that anguish that they've experienced when they are humans.

116
00:11:08,039 --> 00:11:14,480
They just live it perpetually. Like they are not happy with where they are and what the demon king does to them.

117
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:18,399
So I thought that there would be like this turning point where there was like an understanding with Huntrix.

118
00:11:18,399 --> 00:11:29,379
Like these demons like they were one's people and that's still somewhere in there and a lot of them just want to live without that voice in their head reminding them of their biggest mistakes.

119
00:11:29,679 --> 00:11:35,620
That kind of thing. But that never comes. I thought that was where the plot was going at least in a certain to a certain extent, but it's not.

120
00:11:36,019 --> 00:11:44,480
I guess it's just Genu. He is the only one in the entire demon world. Him and his pets. They also are an exception.

121
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:49,980
But it's not a complaint or anything by the way. Like they don't have to go in that direction. It's totally fine. They didn't.

122
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:54,600
I'm just saying I was just kind of surprised because they kind of put the bread crumbs there that I thought that was where they were going.

123
00:11:55,399 --> 00:11:59,240
Anyway, though, I don't have any like big complaints about the movie or anything. I really don't.

124
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:05,879
Even though it's not my cup of tea. It's not my taste. It's not like there was anything in here that I think was wrong or bad.

125
00:12:06,379 --> 00:12:12,600
It's again just not my genre of movie. So it doesn't really appeal to me in a big way.

126
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:18,080
But I didn't have a bad time watching it. I was entertained. I did. That's really about it. See ya.

